messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C04
Scenario title: Family Outing Preparation and Return
Initial workflow description:
Before going out with my child, I get our things together and coordinate with whoever is coming. Afterwards I put things away for next time.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What typically triggers the start of your preparation — for example, a planned date on a calendar, a spontaneous same-day decision, or something else — and roughly how much time before leaving do you begin getting things ready?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Who are the people you coordinate with before the outing, and how do you currently communicate with them to confirm plans or share information?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Can you walk me through the specific items or categories of items you gather before leaving, and does this list change depending on the type of outing or destination?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What do you do if something goes wrong during preparation — for instance, if a key item is missing or a participant can no longer come?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "When you put things away after returning, what specific steps are involved — for example, cleaning, restocking, or storing items in particular places — and how do you know when everything is properly done?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Are there any apps, tools, or systems you already use to support any part of this process, such as a shared calendar, a packing checklist app, or a messaging platform?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Family Outing Preparation and Return with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "accompanying caregiver",
    "venue contact"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "shared family calendar",
    "outing checklist",
    "venue information page",
    "household inventory list"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "outing time",
    "venue information",
    "attendee availability",
    "reusable item inventory"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "confirmed outing plan",
    "packed items list",
    "change notification",
    "restocked bag"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Check the outing time and venue information",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Confirm who will accompany the child",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Prepare the outing checklist",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Check reusable items against the inventory",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Pack and confirm needed items",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Resolve missing items or change the outing plan",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Notify accompanying caregivers of plan changes",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Record used items and restock the bag after returning",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are the venue plan and accompanying caregiver confirmed?",
      "branches": [
        "continue preparation",
        "contact the venue or rearrange the plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are required items available?",
      "branches": [
        "finish packing",
        "obtain an agreed substitute or postpone"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "venue plan changes",
    "accompanying caregiver unavailable",
    "required item missing",
    "used items not restocked"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Create an outing checklist from the confirmed plan."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Draft one consistent plan-change message."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Create restocking reminders from recorded usage."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "one planned outing most weekends in this fictional household",
    "manual_effort": "Checking and packing usually takes about fifteen minutes, excluding travel.",
    "data_availability": "The family keeps an item list but it does not detect physical stock automatically.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "Checklists can be suggested; physical item checks and the decision to change the outing remain with caregivers."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
